  "issue_title": "Harden planner output when an LLM ignores the open PR queue",
  "issue_body": "## Context\n#48 taught the planner to account for the open PR queue when proposing next work. A weaker or adversarial LLM can still ignore the provided queue and emit plans that duplicate or contradict pending PRs. This issue tracks making the planner robust to that \u2014 the output should degrade safely when the model disregards the queue.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Detect when a produced plan ignores or duplicates an open PR from the provided queue\n- [ ] Down-weight or flag plan items that restate work already in flight\n- [ ] Deterministic fallback so an ignored-queue plan still yields a coherent, de-duplicated result\n- [ ] Tests covering: queue provided + honored, queue provided + ignored, empty queue\n\n## Pointers\n`agent/planner.py` (plan assembly + queue handling from #48) and its tests. Follows from #48.\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-03T17:27:23.000Z",
